<title>UK: Boots says to create 5,000 jobs by 2000.</title>
<headline>Boots says to create 5,000 jobs by 2000.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Boots Co Plc, the British high street retailer, said on Thursday it would create 5,000 jobs by 2000, with new staff mainly for its stores.  </p>
<p>Deputy chairman and chief executive Lord Blyth said the company was in the process of expanding its stores, including plans for 40 smaller format Boots The Chemist shops.</p>
<p>He said Boots was not concerned about prospects for the introduction of a minimum wage -- for which the level has not yet been set -- by Britain's newly elected Labour goverment.</p>
<p>&quot;We don't believe it will have a material effect on our business,&quot; he said in a telephone interview. -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
